From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: The taskbar's properties in File Explorer.

The taskbar's properties are pages of the Control Panel inside File
Explorer (taskbarcpl.dll), drawn as Windows 11's Settings, as Windows 10
opens its Settings. The tray says what its pages of the taskbar and the
notification area set, and sets it as their Apply did, by bits
(ArcticTraySettings); it opens Customize of the classic Start menu for them.
It still makes each of its five old pages by itself when asked
(ArcticTrayPropertyPage); a page of explorer's own goes when comctl32 lets
it go. The dialog stays for where the page cannot open.
---
